usage: tego [-h | --help] <command> [<args>]

These are common Tego commands used in various situations:

get started
   start            Set up Tego and connect your first agent
   dashboard        Print its link (Mac: open in browser)

supervise an agent
   run              Run an agent under its rules
   session list     List sessions
   session show     Show what a session did and what Tego refused
   session stop     Stop a running session

write the rules (see also: tego help rules)
   rules create     Create a rules file in a project
   rules edit       Edit a rules file, then check it
   rules check      Check a rules file and show what it enforces
   rules learn      Create a rules file from what a session did

check this machine
   machine check    Check what this machine can enforce
   machine test     Run Tego's self-check

'tego help -a' lists every command, including approvals and live rule changes.
See 'tego help <command>' to read about a specific command.
Manual: https://attention-span.ai/docs/commands/
